From 4fb7dbc353bf02d1af53bcae84c15d43b3c19af9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 6 Aug 2026 23:55:31 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 14/29] batch 256 -> 1024; tunnel keepalive 300s -> 30s

At batch 256 with group_size 8 there are only 32 GRPO groups per step. Over 36
steps reward std was 0.039 against a linear trend of +0.013 total -- the
signal sat well inside the noise. 1024 gives 128 groups, roughly halving
advantage-estimate noise.

Tunnels: ServerAliveInterval/CountMax 15x20 (300s) -> 10x3 (30s). Over a link
with 10-33% packet loss the wedged tunnels accumulated faster than SSH reaped
them -- 22 of 24 dead once, all 24 another time, and the run froze for hours.
4x the rollouts now cross those tunnels, so they need to fail fast.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
